From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lusoris <lusoris@proton.me>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 02:54:28 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] avutil/vulkan: don't release frames to
 VK_QUEUE_FAMILY_IGNORED

On a device with a single queue family, hwcontext_vulkan creates frames
with VK_SHARING_MODE_EXCLUSIVE and tracks them as owned by that family.
ff_vk_frame_barrier() copies the tracked family into srcQueueFamilyIndex,
while every filter and codec caller passes VK_QUEUE_FAMILY_IGNORED as the
new family. The first barrier on such a frame therefore has unequal
indices, which the specification treats as a queue family ownership
transfer, and its destination is VK_QUEUE_FAMILY_IGNORED, which an
exclusive image does not allow (VUID-VkImageMemoryBarrier2-image-09118).

The Khronos validation layer accepts the barrier but records it as a
release that is never acquired. It does not apply the layout transition
and reports every later use of the image against the old layout:
VUID-vkCmdDispatch-imageLayout-00344 and VUID-vkCmdDraw-None-09600 for
shaders that access the image, and
VUID-VkCopyMemoryToImageInfo-dstImageLayout-09059 and
VUID-VkCopyImageToMemoryInfo-srcImageLayout-09064 for the host image
copies in hwupload and hwdownload.

When the caller passes VK_QUEUE_FAMILY_IGNORED and the frame is owned by
a concrete queue family, keep that family as the destination. Equal
indices perform no transfer, and the tracked owner stays the family that
hwcontext_vulkan uses for its own transitions on such devices. Frames on
devices with several queue families are tracked as
VK_QUEUE_FAMILY_IGNORED and are unaffected, as are frames owned by the
external or foreign queue family.

Tested with Mesa lavapipe, which has one queue family, and validation
layer 1.4.363: gblur_vulkan and scdet_vulkan between hwupload and
hwdownload no longer report the four layout errors. Intel ANV, RADV and
the NVIDIA proprietary driver report the same messages as before.

The validation layer gap is reported as
https://github.com/KhronosGroup/Vulkan-ValidationLayers/issues/13405.

Signed-off-by: lusoris <lusoris@proton.me>
---
 libavutil/vulkan.c | 20 ++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libavutil/vulkan.c b/libavutil/vulkan.c
index 3b2cc35bf903bdab3313a10c260377f742e0a22a..c37c108bdc962f8070e37b31b7cc8c41cca1fc5e 100644
--- a/libavutil/vulkan.c
+++ b/libavutil/vulkan.c
@@ -2099,6 +2099,7 @@ void ff_vk_frame_barrier(FFVulkanContext *s, FFVkExecContext *e,
                          uint32_t              new_qf)
 {
     int found = -1;
+    uint32_t src_qf, dst_qf = new_qf;
     AVVkFrame *vkf = (AVVkFrame *)pic->data[0];
     const int nb_images = ff_vk_count_images(vkf);
     for (int i = 0; i < e->nb_frame_deps; i++)
@@ -2108,6 +2109,21 @@ void ff_vk_frame_barrier(FFVulkanContext *s, FFVkExecContext *e,
             break;
         }
 
+    src_qf = found >= 0 ? e->queue_family_dst[found] : vkf->queue_family[0];
+
+    /* Unequal queue family indices define a queue family ownership transfer,
+     * and an exclusive image can only be transferred to a queue family that
+     * exists (or to the external or foreign one), never to
+     * VK_QUEUE_FAMILY_IGNORED (VUID-VkImageMemoryBarrier2-image-09118).
+     * Frames on a device with a single queue family are tracked as owned by
+     * that family, so a caller that asks for no particular family keeps the
+     * current owner: equal indices mean no transfer. */
+    if (new_qf == VK_QUEUE_FAMILY_IGNORED &&
+        src_qf != VK_QUEUE_FAMILY_IGNORED &&
+        src_qf != VK_QUEUE_FAMILY_EXTERNAL &&
+        src_qf != VK_QUEUE_FAMILY_FOREIGN_EXT)
+        dst_qf = src_qf;
+
     for (int i = 0; i < nb_images; i++) {
         bar[*nb_bar] = (VkImageMemoryBarrier2) {
             .sType = VK_STRUCTURE_TYPE_IMAGE_MEMORY_BARRIER_2,
@@ -2118,8 +2134,8 @@ void ff_vk_frame_barrier(FFVulkanContext *s, FFVkExecContext *e,
             .dstAccessMask = new_access,
             .oldLayout = found >= 0 ? e->layout_dst[found] : vkf->layout[0],
             .newLayout = new_layout,
-            .srcQueueFamilyIndex = found >= 0 ? e->queue_family_dst[found] : vkf->queue_family[0],
-            .dstQueueFamilyIndex = new_qf,
+            .srcQueueFamilyIndex = src_qf,
+            .dstQueueFamilyIndex = dst_qf,
             .image = vkf->img[i],
             .subresourceRange = (VkImageSubresourceRange) {
                 .aspectMask = VK_IMAGE_ASPECT_COLOR_BIT,
